From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:32:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: apple-sio: Support every endpoint, cyclic
 transfers and stop
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The SmartIO DMA driver exposed a single channel, the T8010 SPI3 transmit
endpoint, with one fixed shim configuration and one command at a time.
Audio on the A9 needs the MCA endpoints, a shim record per client and
cyclic transfers. Follow iOS 16.7.10's AppleSmartIODMA:

 - One channel per firmware endpoint. The endpoints come from the SIO
   core's per-SoC match data and are handed to the DMA child in its
   platform data: SPI0-3, MCA0-4 and UART0-8 transmit and receive on
   S8000; SPI3 transmit on T8010, the one endpoint in use there so far.
 - op 5 configure carries the shim record (struct apple_sio_dma_config:
   transfer control, timeout, FIFO, trigger, limit, ...) from
   dma_slave_config.peripheral_config, with the firmware's validFIFODepth
   clamp applied to the limit. Without a record the SPI defaults of the
   previous driver are used, so the T8010 touch path sends the same
   configuration as before.
 - op 6 submits a descriptor of 6 header slots and one segment slot per
   segment, split at 4 KiB as iOS does. Commands complete in order with
   a tagged 0x68.
 - Cyclic transfers queue one command per period, at most 16 (the
   firmware has 31 tags per endpoint), and resubmit each period as soon
   as it completes.
 - Terminating sends op 8 stop and waits, bounded, for the queued
   commands to complete before their descriptors are freed. If the
   firmware does not answer, the endpoint's requests are cancelled.

All firmware communication runs in work items with bounded timeouts, so
a stalled coprocessor stalls the stream and never the caller.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux b9740822 (J71t ledger 10.4); the endpoint
 list comes from the SIO core's match data instead of the
 apple,dma-endpoints DT property, and T8010 keeps only SPI3 TX so the
 iPhone 7 SPI2 node (endpoint 0x18) stays on PIO as before. Terminating a
 cyclic transfer stops its period callbacks right away; synchronize
 flushes the stop work instead of waiting on a separate completion.
 Dropped the probe dev_info.]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
